    "why": "The codec output is the input to `Linear(D, d)`, whose weight matrix has a fixed first dimension. A per-token D would mean a per-token weight matrix, which is the per-token parameter table the construction exists to remove. So the dimensional waste is real and cannot be given back without abandoning the idea."
